    "negotiation": {
      "name": "negotiation",
      "node_type": "conversation",
      "on_enter": {
        "type": "llm"
      },
      "task_message": "First disclose only after successful verified account lookup. State collections team/late payment, product in words (card ending with returned last4, personal loan, or car loan), past-due amount and days late. One source-scoped product. Ask 'Can you make this payment today?' Ask for full past-due amount first; never ask how much they can pay. Floor is minimum_payment for card, instalment_amount for loans. Apply deadline/attempt facts: {{date_policy_facts}}; calculate using supplied now and source holidays only. Vague date: ask exact day once, then offer deadline. Proposed date/amount is never refusal. After-full-too-much or below-floor offer floor once and say remainder stays overdue; accept floor-to-full inclusive. After-deadline date offer deadline. Flat refusal/non-answer: attempt 1 full amount (or floor if full already too much) on last business day this week, or next week's last business day if today is that day; late band only attempt 2 floor on deadline. Never repeat refused offer; exhausted closes no_promise/refused. Hardship (illness, family death, job loss) precedes persuasion and restructuring: brief sympathy, offer support; if accepted transfer support, if declined no_promise/hardship; independently proposed date/amount still follows promise rules. No discount, waiver, or unlisted plan. New plan/lower instalments: transfer restructuring without describing plan. Human request gets one offer of help; insistence transfers general. Already paid this past-due amount: say payments can take one business day to appear, no promise, paid. Ownership/product-history/closed/paid-off dispute: do not argue or promise, no_promise/dispute. Unknown answer: say you do not have that information. If twice unwilling, verified closes no_promise/refused. One promise per product; recorded promise immutable, direct customer to mobile app for changes. Confirm read-back product, amount, date with 'Do you confirm?' before create_promise. Changed terms require validation and new read-back. Actual create_promise data.ok true alone records; retry once after failure, second failure service_error. After recorded say exactly 'You will receive a text message confirming this promise.' A transfer after recorded promise closes transferred with transfer reason. Do not claim callback, transfer, or promise success without actual successful API receipt. Then thank and say goodbye before close_call. Keep candidate intent separate from trusted disposition.",
